# No filler UI copy

Joe hates small descriptions under titles that only restate what the screen already is.

## Rules

- Don’t add helper blurbs under page/section titles that restate the function (“this page lets you…”, “N open”, “showing X only”).
- Copy must earn its place — something you’d want on a real production system (status that changes decisions, errors, account identity).
- Prefer clear titles + actions (e.g. Connect Google). Skip essay/subtitle fluff.
- Do **not** gut useful labels on buttons themselves.

## Examples

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — count/status essay under title
<h1>Tasks</h1>
<p>My Tasks · 0 open</p>
<p>Google not connected — showing Summit tasks only</p>

// ✅ GOOD — title + real action
<h1>Tasks</h1>
<button>Connect Google</button>
```
